  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 5's apparent one-quantum dead end is resolved by treating the middle pockets as transit-only: both pieces must cross the center door, continue outward through the outer transit doors, and align from the outer sides at fluid quantities 14 and 16. Level 6 is a three-pocket T-junction where the piece routes upper-left -> shared lower reservoir -> upper-right before aligning. Level 7 expands this to five reservoirs and three pieces; the full solution uses the long central reservoir as a transfer spine, swaps the top-right and lower-left pieces through it, admits the lower-right piece, then simultaneously aligns the three colors at reservoir quantities 5/9/9.",
